When creating or materially editing public-facing UI, first read `docs/27_VECTOR_FRONTEND_UI_UX_SALES_FUNNEL_STANDARD.md`.

Applies to marketing sites, client websites, landing pages, sales funnels, service/product pages, campaign pages, public forms, and CRO variants. Control Plane stays operational, not cinematic.

Before implementation establish audience, primary and secondary conversion, page narrative, brand direction, proof, selected reference principles, component strategy, mobile behavior, and analytics events.

Do not create generic AI-style landing pages: no default purple/blue glow, fake logos, three identical feature cards, oversized radius, or buzzword headlines.

Use shared Vector capability tokens and section variants (`hero-split`, `services-editorial`) without making every client look the same. Do not apply `docs/28` Vector identity (black/blue signal-to-growth chrome) to client Delivery pages. Prefer Outcome → Visual → Explanation → Proof → CTA. Client images and generated media follow `docs/29`.

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Keep essential copy in crawlable HTML. Never fake metrics or invent analytics event names.

Security, privacy, legal, tenant isolation, accessibility, performance, and explicit client requirements override visual experimentation.
